{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792506623,"nonce":"7ZMBn4hUMVpUWCa5/Dqyv3dZoOs=","message":"Adopted Ashui 993438d, which adds reusable CodeEditor/CodeView find and replace. RayDE exposes Find, Replace, Find Next and Find Previous through the command palette, configurable key bindings and each supported keymap. The code editor delegates search controls and edits to Ashui. Default shortcuts are Cmd/Ctrl+F, Cmd+Option+F or Ctrl+H, and Cmd+G/Shift+Cmd+G or F3/Shift+F3. Escape closes and returns focus to the editor.\n\nThe panel is compact, floats at the upper right and uses theme-tinted frosted glass. Bare patterns such as item(\\d+) work with .* enabled; the optional ~/pattern/flags syntax supports explicit Haxe flags. Capture replacements, case/whole-word matching and recoverable regex errors are documented. Tab state retains only search inputs/options while mounted controls, regex subjects and match offsets belong to the active editor owner.\n\nValidation: scripts/check.sh passed, including all keymap conflict checks. Ashui CodeFindTest passed both schemes, its existing CodeComponents passed all 274 checks, and CodeStateLifecycle passed. SNAPSHOT_ONLY=find passed in both schemes with pointer/keyboard interaction, captured single/all replacement, undo, dirty state, inactive view release, restored search state and invalid-regex recovery. Snapshots were visually inspected in dark and light mode. Native bin/rayde and bin/RayDE.app rebuilt against the final pin. The unchanged native library and existing CSS compiler were reused; the bootstrap's temporary duplicate Cargo output was removed, leaving only the dependency's native executable/library cache.\n\nLanded in RayDE commit beb8897; Ashui implementation d20b585 and modifier guard 993438d.","files":null}]}